<BaseLayout title="Legacy content inventory | Internal staging reference">
<meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow" />
<header class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">Unlisted / Temporary working reference</span><h1>Legacy website content inventory.</h1><p>A working record of what appeared on the original Jekyll portfolio, what has been carried into the redesigned site, and what should remain archived. This page is intentionally absent from the public navigation.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/patilbp/patilbp.github.io/tree/archive/legacy-jekyll-2026-10-15" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View frozen original source ↗</a></div></header>
<section class="section"><div class="section-row"><span class="eyebrow">01 / Preserve &amp; refine</span><div><h2>Relevant professional material.</h2><div class="inventory"><div><span class="label keep">Retained</span><h3>Professional experience</h3><p>Honeywell: requirements, reporting, dashboard performance and stakeholder access. Saviant Consulting: machine learning, NLP, automated reporting, AWS deployments, and team responsibilities. Reframed for product and solutions roles without inventing outcomes.</p><a href="https://github.com/patilbp/patilbp.github.io/blob/archive/legacy-jekyll-2026-10-15/_pages/about.md">Original About source ↗</a></div><div><span class="label keep">Retained</span><h3>Education &amp; research</h3><p>University of Pune computer engineering, SDSU graduate studies, Amazon review research, and two 2015/2016 publications about assistive label and text reading. Published in an updated Research presentation.</p><a href="https://github.com/patilbp/patilbp.github.io/blob/archive/legacy-jekyll-2026-10-15/_pages/publications.md">Original Publications source ↗</a></div><div><span class="label pending">Needs supporting material</span><h3>Project case study</h3><p>Customer-care performance measurement was documented as goals, metrics and intended deliverables. Keep as an evidence-qualified draft; replace and expand once project screenshots, individual contributions, and outcomes are confirmed.</p><a href="https://github.com/patilbp/patilbp.github.io/blob/archive/legacy-jekyll-2026-10-15/_pages/projects.md">Original Projects source ↗</a></div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-row"><span class="eyebrow">02 / Archive only</span><div><h2>Not appropriate for the new public narrative.</h2><div class="inventory"><div><span class="label archive">Excluded</span><h3>Outdated résumé template</h3><p>The old CV route included sample GitHub University education and work history. These are placeholders, not user credentials, so they will not migrate.</p><a href="https://github.com/patilbp/patilbp.github.io/blob/archive/legacy-jekyll-2026-10-15/_pages/cv.md">Original CV source ↗</a></div><div><span class="label archive">Archived</span><h3>Historical personal content</h3><p>Photography and cooking notes remain in the archive. Personal interests can be added back selectively if they help tell the professional story.</p><a href="https://github.com/patilbp/patilbp.github.io/blob/archive/legacy-jekyll-2026-10-15/_pages/personal.md">Original Personal source ↗</a></div><div><span class="label archive">Archived</span><h3>Old navigation and theme</h3><p>Legacy Jekyll styling and miscellaneous resources remain accessible in GitHub history but will not clutter the new top-level navigation.</p><a href="https://github.com/patilbp/patilbp.github.io/tree/archive/legacy-jekyll-2026-10-15/_pages">Original pages folder ↗</a></div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-row"><span class="eyebrow">03 / Release policy</span><div><h2>Proof over buzzwords.</h2><p>Preserve verifiable experience and technical accomplishments; label proposed solutions and research interests clearly; request accurate outcomes before making impact claims. The archived branch is the immutable baseline for future comparison.</p></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
